          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0082",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The following [[p0]] example returns the state of a calendar at the specified time.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "get-calendar-state"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0083",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Output:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0084",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For more information, see [[p0]] in the [[p1]]AWS Systems Manager User Guide[[p2]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "Getting the state of a change calendar",
            "href": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/change-calendar-getstate.html"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0085",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Output¶",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0086",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "State -> (string)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0087",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The state of the calendar. An [[p0]] calendar indicates that actions are allowed to proceed, and a [[p1]] calendar indicates that actions aren’t allowed to proceed.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "OPEN"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "CLOSED"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0088",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Possible values:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0089",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "OPEN"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0090",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "CLOSED"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0091",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "AtTime -> (string)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0092",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The time, as an [[p0]] string, that you specified in your command. If you don’t specify a time, [[p1]] uses the current time.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "ISO 8601",
            "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "GetCalendarState"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0093",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "NextTransitionTime -> (string)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0094",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The time, as an [[p0]] string, that the calendar state will change. If the current calendar state is [[p1]] , [[p2]] indicates when the calendar state changes to [[p3]] , and vice-versa.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "ISO 8601",
            "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "OPEN"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "NextTransitionTime"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "CLOSED"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
